            }}
            th, td {{
                padding: 12px 15px;
                text-align: left;
                border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
            }}
            th {{
                background-color: var(--primary);
                color: white;
            }}
            tr:nth-child(even) {{
                background-color: #f2f2f2;
            }}
            .finding-box {{
                background-color: #e8f4f8;
                border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
                padding: 15px 20px;
                margin: 20px 0;
                border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
            }}
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <div class="container">
            <header>
                <h1>Global Cost of Living Crisis Index 2026</h1>
                <p class="subtitle">A Comparative Analysis of Economic Stress Across Cities and Regions</p>
                <p><strong>Target Audience:</strong> Policy Analysts & Economic Researchers</p>
            </header>

            <section id="executive-overview">
                <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
                <p>This report provides an analytical examination of cost-of-living pressures, affordability gaps, and economic stress indicators across 80 major cities worldwide in 2026. The aim is to supply decision-makers with data-driven insights into housing affordability, inflation impacts, and the characteristics of high-crisis urban centers.</p>

                <div class="kpi-container">
                    <div class="kpi-card">
                        <div class="kpi-label">Median Cost of Living</div>
                        <div class="kpi-value">{median_col_index:.1f}</div>
                        <div class="kpi-desc">Index (NY = 100)</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi-card">
                        <div class="kpi-label">Avg Rent-to-Salary</div>
                        <div class="kpi-value">{avg_rent_to_salary:.1f}%</div>
                        <div class="kpi-desc">Share of Income</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi-card">
                        <div class="kpi-label">Purchasing Power Gap</div>
                        <div class="kpi-value">{purchasing_power_gap:.1f}</div>
                        <div class="kpi-desc">Max - Min Index</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi-card">
                        <div class="kpi-label">High-Crisis Cities</div>
                        <div class="kpi-value">{high_crisis_count}</div>
                        <div class="kpi-desc">Tier {max_crisis_tier} Designation</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="kpi-card">
                        <div class="kpi-label">Avg Inflation 2025</div>
                        <div class="kpi-value">{avg_inflation:.2f}%</div>
                        <div class="kpi-desc">Annual Rate</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="regional-comparison">
                <h2>Regional Cost-of-Living Comparison</h2>
                <p>An analysis of cost-of-living indices against rent indices reveals distinct regional clusters. Cities far from their regional clusters represent critical outliers requiring specialized policy interventions.</p>

                <div class="chart-container">
                    <img src="data:image/png;base64,{chart1_b64}" alt="Regional Comparison Chart">
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="affordability-analysis">
                <h2>Affordability and Rent Burden Analysis</h2>
                <p>The rent-to-salary ratio is the most direct indicator of housing affordability. Values exceeding 50% indicate severe structural imbalances between local wages and housing costs.</p>

                <div class="chart-container">
                    <img src="data:image/png;base64,{chart2_b64}" alt="Rent Burden Chart">
