                <div class="finding-box">
                    <strong>Critical Insight:</strong> The cities with the highest rent-to-salary ratios highlight severe housing affordability crises where local purchasing power is significantly constrained by rent costs, even in regions with ostensibly high nominal salaries.
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="crisis-tier-profiling">
                <h2>Crisis Tier Profiling</h2>
                <p>By grouping cities into crisis tiers, we observe stark contrasts between affluent high-cost cities (high living costs but matched by extremely high purchasing power) and true high-crisis cities (where high relative costs meet low purchasing power).</p>

                <div class="chart-container">
                    <img src="data:image/png;base64,{chart3_b64}" alt="Crisis Tier Chart">
                </div>

