                    <li><strong>Urgent Housing Interventions:</strong> Cities in the top decile of the rent-to-salary ratio require immediate policy interventions such as rent stabilization, affordable housing mandates, or targeted wage subsidies.</li>
                    <li><strong>Purchasing Power Disparity:</strong> The large purchasing power gap ({purchasing_power_gap:.1f} index points) indicates a fractured global economy where nominal affordability masks severe local hardship.</li>
                    <li><strong>Systemic Vulnerabilities:</strong> The {high_crisis_count} cities in the highest crisis tier should be prioritized for international aid or structural economic reform, particularly those also suffering from high oil shock exposure and elevated inflation.</li>
                    <li><strong>Outlier Management:</strong> Policymakers must focus on cities that deviate negatively from their regional norms, as they may suffer from hyper-local structural issues rather than broad macro-economic trends.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </div>
    </body>
    </html>
